  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thandanani AIDS Programme: Community Based OVC Care &amp; Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a development project and aims improve the quality of life of OVC in KZN. The project will attain this through  building the capacity of 19 to 20 communities in Msunduzi (Pietermaritzburg) and Richmond in the Midlands of KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa to respond to the basic material, physical, cognitive and emotional needs of their orphans and vulnerable children (OVC).  
The project activities include promotion of the livelihood security of OVC through Food security, shelter, health monitoring  and  life skills activities. Other activities include early learning centre support and development, advocacy for fee exemption and child rights, provision of school resources, monitoring school attendance and performance of OVC, counselling, caregiver placement and memory box initiatives. Through this developmental approach, Thandanani endeavours to empower and support community based volunteer teams in the provision of care and support to OVC.Project is aimed at strengthening the capacity of those involved in OVC care to the point where they can independently respond to the needs of OVC within their community. 
In this way, they aim bring about fundamental changes at the individual, household and community level that alter the basic conditions of existence and assist individuals, households and communities to break the cycle of poverty that entraps them.</narrative>
  </description>
